Verification (bundled pack build artefact)

**Deliverable:** `tests/main-street/BundledPackBuildArtefact.test.ts` (4 tests, unit project). It drives the real Vite production build (the `vite build` half of `npm run build`, the same build-to-temp-`outDir` pattern as `tests/deploy/vite-base-gating.test.ts`) into a fresh temp directory and asserts the emitted bundle embeds:
- the residential pack manifest verbatim (`main-street-residential-pack`, `gameId`, `cards.csv`);
- the residential `cards.csv` verbatim (header + `biz-ms-residential-property-mgmt`);
- every asset the manifest declares (each is inlined as a `data:image/png` URI or emitted as a standalone file);
- no `tce-packs://` URL in any emitted asset chunk.

Because the temp `outDir` starts empty and nothing copies `packs/` into it (asserted: no `dist/packs`), a green run proves the `import.meta.glob` bundled source baked the committed pack into the bundle with no manual `<contentDir>/packs/` copy step.

**Existing registry contract test (independent re-run, green):** `tests/main-street/PackSourceRegistry.test.ts` (18 tests) — source ordering, additive registration, unknown path / empty registry / rejecting-source total degradation, real-glob resolution of the committed pack, URL→packs-path mapping, and end-to-end loader wiring with a `fetch` spy proving the bundled path makes no `tce-packs://` request.

**AC coverage:** all four verification-child ACs met (build-artefact proof; additive registry over a non-Electron source; no `tce-packs://` request; deterministic unit-project tests that fail on regression).

**Assumption recorded:** the artefact test invokes Vite's production build programmatically into a temp `outDir` rather than the shell `npm run build` so the repo `dist/` is never touched and tests stay isolated; the `tsc --noEmit` type gate is covered by the build/CI pipeline and the unit suite.
